Obey two Vulkan device limits the backend was ignoring.

Both were found with the validation layer on an Intel Arc Pro, where the omni
lane's diffusion transformer and vocoder produced VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST within a
few dispatches. Neither is device-specific in nature; both are spec violations
that most desktop drivers happen to tolerate.

1. Storage buffer offsets were not aligned.

   A tensor's offset inside its pool goes straight to vkUpdateDescriptorSets as
   a storage buffer offset, so it must be a multiple of
   minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment. The pools were built with nonCoherentAtomSize
   instead, which is the flush granularity of mapped memory -- a different limit
   answering a different question.

   On most desktop drivers the two coincide at 64 and nothing shows. This Arc
   reports nonCoherentAtomSize 1 and minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment 64, so every
   offset was arbitrary: VUID-VkWriteDescriptorSet-descriptorType-00328 on every
   descriptor write.

   VulkanDevice::bufferAlignment() is the maximum of the two, and the four pools
   that hand out tensor offsets now use it.

2. 16-bit access to UNIFORM blocks was never enabled.

   checkFP16 enables storageBuffer16BitAccess, which covers SSBOs. The shaders
   also put 16-bit members in uniform blocks, and that is a separate feature:
   uniformAndStorageBuffer16BitAccess. Without it every such read is undefined
   behaviour -- VUID-RuntimeSpirv-uniformAndStorageBuffer16BitAccess-06332 -- and
   the failure surfaces as a lost device with no other diagnostic.

   Enabled on both paths, and only when the device reports it, so a device that
   supports 16-bit storage buffers but not 16-bit uniforms is unaffected.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX. With both in place the device is no longer lost and every
operator runs on the GPU, but the Qwen2.5-Omni token2wav graph still produces
noise rather than speech, identically at fp16 and fp32 -- so there is at least
one more defect in the buffer path's operators, and it is not a precision
problem. The patch is kept because the two violations above are real and would
mislead the next attempt, not because it makes the backend usable here.

diff --git a/source/backend/vulkan/buffer/backend/VulkanBackend.cpp b/source/backend/vulkan/buffer/backend/VulkanBackend.cpp
index 03d163b..b237dba 100644
